# The app has no build step and no dependencies, so there is little to ignore.
# What is here is mostly a safety net: this repo is public on GitHub, and the hard
# rule in CLAUDE.md is that none of the user's financial data may reach source.

# --- Financial data (the rule that matters) ---------------------------------
# The Sheet is the only store. Nothing exported from it belongs in the repo, and
# the Transactions / ledger screens both offer CSV export straight to disk.
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.ods

# --- Google credentials ------------------------------------------------------
# Only the OAuth *Client ID* is used, and it lives in localStorage, not a file.
# A client_secret*.json downloaded from Google Cloud Console has no business here.
client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
*.pem

# --- Local connection defaults ------------------------------------------------
# config/.env prefills the Settings fields on a dev copy. It is local-only: the
# hosted site has no such file. config/.env.example IS tracked — it is the template
# and carries placeholders only, so the negation below must stay after the patterns.
.env
.env.*
!config/.env.example

# --- Node, if npx is used to serve ------------------------------------------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log
.npm/

# --- Test scratch ------------------------------------------------------------
# Golden baselines and the smoke harness ARE committed — they are the safety net.
# Only throwaway output is ignored.
test/screenshots/
test/tmp/
*.local.json

# --- Editor and OS -----------------------------------------------------------
# .vscode/settings.json is tracked deliberately; nothing else in there is.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
*.code-workspace
.idea/
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*~
*.swp
